@* Replaces paypalsubscription.aspx. The route is the LITERAL legacy URL, case for case: it is
   configured externally (it is the URL a portal's subscription/cancellation links point at), so it
   cannot be renamed. Blazor route matching is case insensitive, so every casing that resolved
   before resolves now.

   The page had no markup at all - paypalsubscription.aspx was a single @@ Page directive and the
   code behind always ended in Response.Redirect - so this component renders nothing in the normal
   flow. The whole of OnLoad lives in PayPalSubscription.razor.cs and finishes by navigating to the
   built PayPal URL. The paragraph below is only reachable when the redirect itself failed (the
   catch path of the original), which previously produced DNN's error page. *@

@page "/admin/Sales/paypalsubscription.aspx"
@namespace DotNetNuke.Modules.Admin.Sales

@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(this.RedirectFailureMessage))
{
    <p class="NormalRed">@this.RedirectFailureMessage</p>
}
